From c57878a5bb5b37f4a5372be470fb81efb560d131 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:20:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 111/112] test: add the signet_blocksig fuzz target for both
 signet block signature parsers

No fuzz target reached CheckSignetPQBlock: the signet target runs on the
default signet, which has neither block signature rule. signet_blocksig runs
on a custom signet with -signetpqblock and -signetslhblock, once with both
rules from height 1 and once from the highest height, where the checks run
only for the -debug=validation verdict, which the target enables.

Blocks are either deserialized as they come or built from the fuzzer's
choices: a coinbase with a BIP34 height or other bytes, and outputs near the
forms the rules look at (the SLH output of every length around 7865, with a
byte of its prefix changed or cut short; the cut SLH output; witness
commitments with an ML-DSA-44 push or other bytes after them; OP_RETURN
pushes; prefixes of the SLH output). It checks that a block committing to a
height of 0 to 16 passes both rules below their height and, from 1 on,
neither from height 1, as no fuzzer can sign for these keys; and that a
signature span is exactly 7856 bytes of an output at c - 1 for which the
message exists.
